{"esquema":1,"id":149,"gbif":1310145,"nome":"Agelaia pallipes","autoria":"(Olivier, 1791) ","grupo":"animal_peconhento","taxonomia":{"reino":"Animalia","filo":"Arthropoda","classe":"Insecta","ordem":"Hymenoptera","familia":"Vespidae","genero":"Agelaia"},"populares":[{"nome":"Vespa-Carniceira","idioma":"por"},{"nome":"Neotropical social wasp","idioma":"en"}],"sinonimos":[{"nome":"Polybia lutea","autoria":"Ducke, 1904","categoria":"SPECIES"},{"nome":"Vespa pallipes","autoria":"Olivier, 1791","categoria":"SPECIES"}],"origem_estabelecimento":"nativa","distribuicao_br":"registros_brasileiros_dispersos","ecologia":{"endemismo_br":null,"biomas":[],"forma_vida":null,"estrato_florestal":null,"categoria_mma":null,"fonte_checklist":"Catálogo Taxonômico da Fauna do Brasil","consulta":9},"iucn":{"categoria":"NE","consulta":10},"recorte":{"dentro":true,"n_al":136,"n_al_exato":130,"n_br":1038,"n_br_com_uf":493,"n_bioma_amazonia":108,"n_ma_oeste44":12,"consulta_bioma":11,"fracao_com_uf":0.27586206896551724,"fracao_total":0.13102119460500963,"predominio":"nao_predominante","motivo":"Dentro do recorte: 136 registro(s) do GBIF na Amazônia Legal (mínimo exigido: 20). Dos 493 registro(s) brasileiros com UF atribuída, 28% estão na Amazônia Legal. 545 registro(s) do Brasil não têm UF e ficam fora dessa conta; contando-os, a fração cai para 13%. Predomínio amazônico: não, nem mesmo só entre os registros com UF. Consulta ao GBIF em 2026-11-07. Distribuição conhecida não comprova a procedência de nenhum estudo.","consulta":12,"origem_inclusao":"Tox-Prot (UniProt)","correspondencia_gbif":"EXACT","confianca_gbif":100},"uf":{"AC":36,"AL":7,"AM":19,"AP":2,"CE":10,"DF":21,"GO":13,"MA":17,"MG":62,"MS":1,"MT":1,"PA":28,"PB":12,"PE":62,"PI":11,"PR":15,"RN":2,"RO":20,"RR":6,"RS":2,"SP":139,"TO":7},"bacias":[{"id":"BAC:JURUA_PURUS","nome":"Juruá–Purus–Acre","n":37,"consulta":0},{"id":"BAC:MADEIRA","nome":"Madeira–Guaporé–Aripuanã","n":22,"consulta":1},{"id":"BAC:TOCANTINS","nome":"Tocantins–Araguaia–Guamá","n":21,"consulta":2},{"id":"BAC:NEGRO","nome":"Rio Negro–Branco","n":20,"consulta":3},{"id":"BAC:GURUPI_MEARIM","nome":"Gurupi–Turiaçu–Pindaré–Mearim (Amazônia Maranhense)","n":9,"consulta":4},{"id":"BAC:AMAZONAS_TROMBETAS","nome":"Médio e Baixo Amazonas–Trombetas–Jari–Amapá","n":7,"consulta":5},{"id":"BAC:TAPAJOS","nome":"Tapajós–Juruena–Teles Pires","n":6,"consulta":6},{"id":"BAC:XINGU","nome":"Xingu–Iriri","n":2,"consulta":7},{"id":"BAC:SOLIMOES","nome":"Alto Solimões–Javari–Içá–Japurá","n":1,"consulta":8}],"contexto_biocultural":[],"imagens":[{"arquivo":"imagens/1310145/1.jpg","largura":500,"altura":500,"autor":"Eli","licenca":"CC BY","pagina":"https://www.gbif.org/occurrence/6334163976","instituicao":"iNaturalist","pais":"BR","v":"498586","foco":[42.5,56.9],"nota":0.998}],"cobertura":{"compostos":0,"compostos_lotus":0,"compostos_nubbe":0,"compostos_npatlas":0,"consulta_lotus":13,"toxinas_fonte":2,"consulta_uniprot":14,"consulta_nubbe":null,"consulta_npatlas":null},"total_moleculas":2,"paginas_moleculas":[],"moleculas":[{"id":12,"nome":"Protonectin","tipo":"peptideo","classe":null,"familia":"MCD family. Protonectin subfamily","formula":null,"massa":null,"uniprot":"P69437","comprimento_aa":12,"estrutura":null,"n_publicacoes":7,"n_atividades":0,"aprovado":false,"afirmacao":{"id":12,"tipo":"funcao_toxina","estado":"candidato","evidencia":"base_curada","indice":0.5,"refs":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6],"procedencia":"nao_declarada","passagem":"Potent antimicrobial peptide that acts by disruption of the integrity of the membrane, thanks to its alpha-helical conformation in the membrane (PubMed:23836163, PubMed:26209560). Shows potent antibacterial activity against both Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria (MIC=4-128 uM) (By similarity) (PubMed:15225564, PubMed:20600225, PubMed:23836163, PubMed:28299840). Is also active on yeasts (mainly tested on Candida cells, MIC=4-128 uM), by disrupting the membrane integrity and inducing the production of cellular reactive oxygen species (ROS) (By similarity) (PubMed:26209560, PubMed:28299840). In addition, inhibits the formation of yeast biofilms and kills the adherent fungi cells (PubMed:26209560). Has relative binding specificity with the yeast polysaccharide laminarin, but not with the yeast polysaccharide mannan (PubMed:26209560). Also has mast cell degranulation activity, and induces a potent chemotaxis in polymorphonucleated leukocyte (PMNL) cells (PubMed:15052574, PubMed:15225564, PubMed:20600225). Its mast cell degranulation activity may be related to the activation of G protein-coupled receptors in mast cells as well as interaction with other proteins located in cell endosomal membranes in the mast cells (By similarity). Shows weak hemolytic activity (EC(50)=80 uM) (PubMed:15052574, PubMed:15225564, PubMed:20600225, PubMed:28299840). In vivo, exhibits anti-nociceptive activity (at 8 nmol, intracerebroventricular injection) (PubMed:34090029). Is toxic to cancer (Melanoma MM96L, and colorectal cancer HCT 116) and non-cancer cell lines (HaCaT, and HEK293) (By similarity). Is also much more toxic to metastatic breast cancer cell lines (MDA-MB-231) than to non-cancerous epithelial breast cell lines (MCF-10) (By similarity) (PubMed:15052574, PubMed:15225564, PubMed:20600225, PubMed:23836163, PubMed:26209560, PubMed:28299840, PubMed:34090029) Has higher chemotactic activity for polymorphonucleated leukocyte (PMNL) cells than protonectin. Has no antibacterial, and mast cell degranulation activities alone, but its presence potentiates protonectin on these two activities (PubMed:20600225). Has no hemolytic activity alone, but its presence potentiates protonectin activity on both rat and human erythrocytes (PubMed:20600225, PubMed:34090029). Has no cytotoxic activity towards both metastatic breast cancer cells (MDA-MB-231) and epithelial breast cells (MCF-10), and its presence does not (or very weakly) change protonectin cytotoxicity on these cells (PubMed:34090029)","experimental":true}},{"id":13,"nome":"Agelaia-MPI","tipo":"peptideo","classe":null,"familia":"MCD family. Mastoparan subfamily","formula":null,"massa":null,"uniprot":"P69436","comprimento_aa":14,"estrutura":null,"n_publicacoes":3,"n_atividades":0,"aprovado":false,"afirmacao":{"id":13,"tipo":"funcao_toxina","estado":"candidato","evidencia":"base_curada","indice":0.5,"refs":[0,1,7],"procedencia":"nao_declarada","passagem":"Antimicrobial peptide with potent activity towards many Gram-positive, and Gram-negative bacteria, as well as yeasts (C.albicans, C.tropicalis, and C.neoformans) (By similarity) (PubMed:30974767). Inhibits biofilm formation of A.baumannii and Staphylococcus spp. bacteria (PubMed:30974767). Also shows potent mast cell degranulation activity and potent hemolytic activity of rat erythrocytes (PubMed:15052574, PubMed:15225564). Its mast cell degranulation activity may be related to the activation of G protein-coupled receptors in mast cells as well as interaction with other proteins located in cell endosomal membranes in the mast cells (By similarity). Does not show chemotaxis for polymorphonucleated leukocytes (PMNL) (PubMed:15052574, PubMed:15225564). In vivo, has antinociceptive activity when intracerebroventricularly injected into mice (By similarity)","experimental":true}}],"refs":[{"doi":"10.1002/rcm.1382","pmid":"15052574","titulo":"Structural characterization of novel chemotactic and mastoparan peptides from the venom of the social wasp Agelaiapallipes pallipes by high-performance liquid chromatography/electrospray ionization tandem mass spectrometry.","autores":["Mendes MA","Monson de Souza B","Delazari dos Santos L","et al."],"revista":"Rapid Commun Mass Spectrom","ano":2004,"aviso":null,"resolvida":true,"tipo_obra":"journal-article"},{"doi":"10.1016/j.toxicon.2004.04.009","pmid":"15225564","titulo":"Structural and biological characterization of two novel peptides from the venom of the neotropical social wasp Agelaia pallipes pallipes.","autores":["Mendes MA","de Souza BM","Marques MR","et al."],"revista":"Toxicon","ano":2004,"aviso":null,"resolvida":true,"tipo_obra":"journal-article"},{"doi":"10.1016/j.toxicon.2010.06.011","pmid":"20600225","titulo":"Protonectin (1-6): a novel chemotactic peptide from the venom of the social wasp Agelaia pallipes pallipes.","autores":["Baptista-Saidemberg NB","Saidemberg DM","de Souza BM","et al."],"revista":"Toxicon","ano":2010,"aviso":null,"resolvida":true,"tipo_obra":"journal-article"},{"doi":"10.1128/aac.02311-12","pmid":"23836163","titulo":"Membrane perturbation action mode and structure-activity relationships of Protonectin, a novel antimicrobial peptide from the venom of the neotropical social wasp Agelaia pallipes pallipes.","autores":["Wang K","Dang W","Yan J","et al."],"revista":"Antimicrob Agents Chemother","ano":2013,"aviso":null,"resolvida":true,"tipo_obra":"journal-article"},{"doi":"10.1016/j.bbamem.2015.07.008","pmid":"26209560","titulo":"Antimicrobial peptide protonectin disturbs the membrane integrity and induces ROS production in yeast cells.","autores":["Wang K","Dang W","Xie J","et al."],"revista":"Biochim Biophys Acta","ano":2015,"aviso":null,"resolvida":true,"tipo_obra":"journal-article"},{"doi":"10.1002/psc.2989","pmid":"28299840","titulo":"Antimicrobial activity and stability of protonectin with D-amino acid substitutions.","autores":["Qiu S","Zhu R","Zhao Y","et al."],"revista":"J Pept Sci","ano":2017,"aviso":null,"resolvida":true,"tipo_obra":"journal-article"},{"doi":"10.1016/j.jcis.2021.05.115","pmid":"34090029","titulo":"Protonectin peptides target lipids, act at the interface and selectively kill metastatic breast cancer cells while preserving morphological integrity.","autores":["Batista Martins D","Fadel V","Oliveira FD","et al."],"revista":"J Colloid Interface Sci","ano":2021,"aviso":null,"resolvida":true,"tipo_obra":"journal-article"},{"doi":"10.3390/toxins11040216","pmid":"30974767","titulo":"Antimicrobial and Antibiofilm Effects of Peptides from Venom of Social W